
Simple San Simon Functional Web Browser
=======================================

It is a computer desktop program for rendering web pages.
One nice thing is that it is written with Haskell, a purely funcional programming language.
It supports a generic markup language (like ~ html or xhtml or xml) and part of CSS.

The GUI uses GTK 4 through haskell-gi. There are two programs:

  * 3sfwbrowser: the web browser.
  * 3sfboxer: shows the box tree of the formatting structure of a page, and
    the CSS properties (specified, computed, used and actual values) of
    each box.


Requirements
------------

  * GHC (tested with 9.10.3) and cabal-install (tested with 3.12)
  * GTK 4, GObject Introspection, libgd and libcurl, with their development
    files. On Debian/Ubuntu:

	sudo apt install pkg-config libgtk-4-dev libgirepository1.0-dev libgd-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev

uuagc (the attribute grammar compiler) and the haskell-gi bindings are
fetched and built by cabal; the first build takes a while.


To build
--------

From the root of the repository:

	cabal update
	cabal build all


Configuration
-------------

The browser reads its configuration from '~/.3SFWebBrowser/', a copy of the
'config' directory of the repository:

	cp -r config ~/.3SFWebBrowser

Then edit '~/.3SFWebBrowser/dbf' and set the paths of 'User_Agent_Stylesheet'
(the html4.css file) and 'User_Stylesheet' (any css file, or remove the line).
Downloaded images and stylesheets are saved at '~/.3SFWebBrowser/tmp/'.

Without that directory the browser still starts, using './config/html4.css',
but it can not show images.


Web browser (3sfwbrowser)
-------------------------

From the root of the repository:

	cabal run 3sfwbrowser
	cabal run 3sfwbrowser -- file://$PWD/examples/test3.html   # open a page at start

Type a URL and press Enter or "Get". "Update" recomputes the layout,
"=<<" and ">>=" go backward and forward in the history. Click a link to
follow it. The stylesheets can be changed in the Settings menu.


Boxer GUI (3sfboxer)
--------------------

From the root of the repository (it reads './config/html4.css'):

	cabal run 3sfboxer

Type a URL (for example file:///<path to the repository>/examples/test1.html,
which is the default) and press Enter or the "Dibujar" button. Click a box
to see its properties.


For more information
--------------------

